    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="24">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 24</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="164" ed="#liebermann"/>Ond se þe yrfe bycge on gewitnesse ⁊ hit eft tymon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.3"/> scyle, þonne onfó se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.2"/> his þe he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.6"/> hit ǽr ætbohte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.9"/>, beo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.10"/> he swa freoh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.11"/> swa ðeow, swa hweðer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.12"/> he sy.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.8"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-ld"><pb n="164" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ðæm ðe yrfe bycgaþ. Se ðe yrfe bycge on gewitnysse ⁊ hit eft mon teaman scyle, ðonne onfó se his ðe he hit ær ætbohte, sy swa þeowe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.1"/> swa freoh, hweþer he sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-ot"><pb n="164" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se ðe yrfe bycgge on . . . tieman scyle, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> onfo se his ðe he hit . . ., . . . swa freoh . . ., . . . hweðer he sie.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.star"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="165" ed="#liebermann"/>De<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.4"/> illis qui pecus emunt per testimonium. Qui aliquid emit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.5"/>, emat cum testibus. Et si appellandum sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.6-2"/> inde, recipiat hoc (uenditor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.7"/> suus), a quo emit, sit liber sit seruus, sit quod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.oe.8-2"/> sit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="24" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="140" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ðæm ðe yrfe bycgaþ.]<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#IIAs_24.attnote.fn.13"/> Ond se þe yrfe bycge on gewitnesse ⁊ hit eft tymon<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#IIAs_24.attnote.fn.14"/> scyle, þonne onfó se his þe he hit ǽr ætbohte, beo he swa<ptr type="editorNote" n="15" target="#IIAs_24.attnote.fn.15"/> freoh swa ðeow, swa hweðer he sy.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="165" ed="#liebermann"/>(Von denen, die Vieh kaufen. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi>) Und wer Vieh unter Zeugenschaft<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.de.1"/> kauft und es nachher [im Anefang verklagt,] zur Gewähr schieben muss: dann übernehme es der [Gewährsmann], dem er es zuvor abgekauft hat, sei dieser frei oder unfrei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_24.lnote.de.2"/>, wie er auch sei.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of those who buy cattle. Ld) And whoever buys cattle with witnesses and afterwards [being sued by attachment] has to vouch it to warranty: then let the [warrantor] from whom he previously bought it take it over, whether he be free or unfree, whichever he may be.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="141" ed="#attenborough"/>And if anyone buys cattle in the presence of a witness, and afterwards has to vouch it to warranty, then he from whom he has bought it shall receive it back again<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_24.attnote.n.1"/>, whether he be a slave<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_24.attnote.n.2"/> or a freeman—whichever he may be.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="422" ed="#whitelock"/>And he who buys livestock with a witness, and has to vouch to warranty afterwards—then he from whom he bought it is to take it back, whether he be slave or free, whichever he is. 24. 1. And there is to be no trading on Sundays; if then anyone does it, he is to forfeit the goods and pay 30 shillings fine.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">After this, Ot is legible only for the words ‘Gif mi’ (perhaps the beginning of 25).</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æt <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æt on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">b. h. <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">b. h. on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hwe <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hwe written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">diese Rubrik bringt schon hinter Rb.</hi> 22 <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> Si quis emat cum testibus; ne fiat negotiatio die dominica; et qui hoc uel illud presumpserit <hi rend="italic">MHk;</hi> Quod emptio fiat c. t.; et ne neg. f. die solis [so. <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur Brti</hi>] <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">T already gives this rubric after Rb. 22; Si quis emat cum testibus; ne fiat negotiatio die dominica; et qui hoc uel illud presumpserit MHk; Quod emptio fiat c. t.; et ne neg. f. die solis [so. on an erasure Brti] Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">emat <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">emat MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i. sit <hi rend="italic">RMHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i. sit RMHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u. s. <hi rend="italic">nicht Lond, spätere Zufügung der übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u. s. not in Lond; a later addition in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">s. q. s. <hi rend="italic">fehlt KOr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s. q. s. lacking in KOr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ferner nur</hi> Gif mi [<hi rend="italic">Anfang von</hi> 25?] <hi rend="italic">lesbar</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">beyond this only Gif mi [beginning of 25?] legible</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Anefang 10. 12. 14 f.; Kaufzeugen 7</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Anefang 10. 12. 14 f.; Kaufzeugen 7</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_24.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> unfrei 21 c. 22</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> unfrei 21 c. 22</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_24.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">209</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">And with it, the responsibility for proving whence he obtained it (see II Athlr. cap. 8, 9).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_24.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">209</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Contrast Ine, cap. 47.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_24.attnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><label>bycgaþ</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_24.attnote.fn.14" n="14" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><label>tymon</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mon teaman</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_24.attnote.fn.15" n="15" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><label>swa</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">sy swa</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
